        "title": "feat(signal): add guided setup wizard",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSignal setup previously made users assemble a working `signal-cli` transport by hand before OpenClaw could receive messages. This PR adds a guided Signal setup flow that can create a loopback Docker helper, connect to an existing Signal server, or keep using native `signal-cli`, then records the selected transport so status, probe, send, and receive paths use the correct API shape.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe implementation keeps Signal-specific setup inside the Signal plugin and adds only the narrow core/SDK seams needed for plugin-owned setup. It adds Docker/native/existing-server setup choices, account-scoped `apiMode`, setup rollback semantics, a small QR terminal SDK subpath, status/probe readiness output, and docs for the supported config and setup paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can run `openclaw channels add`, choose the recommended Signal Docker path, scan/link through the wizard, and get a saved `channels.signal` config without editing JSON by hand. Operators keep the existing-server escape hatch, mixed-account transport modes are preserved, and the Docker setup image is pinned by digest instead of executing a mutable tag.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Signal setup wizard E2E passed earlier in a scratch setup pane using scratch config under `/tmp/openclaw-signal-real-tui`; no real user config was touched and no manual Signal messages were sent.\n- Scratch gateway probe proof reached the Signal channel through the scratch config and gateway path after setup wrote `channels.signal` with `httpUrl` and container `apiMode`.\n- Docker setup now uses the pinned image `bbernhard/signal-cli-rest-api:0.100@sha256:2399d449123cdad56c4d859277e3b9127e1a00c4d2ab4601c239882609286cf8`; `docker buildx imagetools inspect bbernhard/signal-cli-rest-api:0.100` reported that manifest-list digest.\n- Existing Signal server setup and Docker setup are covered by focused setup tests, including QR/link handling, account linking validation, setup cancellation rollback, transport classification, and pinned Docker args.\n- Account-scoped `apiMode` routing is covered for sends, typing, read receipts, reactions, probe/check, and receive streaming.\n\nReviewer-checkable validation:\n\n- `codex review --base origin/main` completed clean on pushed head `72899d71973ca743f7d357f1c7ba0b27dfa935b3`.\n- Independent cold review of `origin/main...HEAD` completed clean on the same head.\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/signal/src/setup-core.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts` passed.\n- `timeout 180s env OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 OPENCLAW_VITEST_NO_OUTPUT_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-signal.config.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts -t \"creates Signal containers with a restart policy\" --reporter verbose` passed: 1 selected test.\n- `timeout 180s env OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 OPENCLAW_VITEST_NO_OUTPUT_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-signal.config.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts -t \"creates a Docker container when the setup wizard selects container mode|creates a Docker container when switching from an existing Signal server|does not save failed Docker container setup\" --reporter verbose` passed: 2 selected tests.\n- `pnpm docs:list` passed.\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx docs/channels/signal.md` passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nNo browser screenshot is included because this PR changes CLI/setup, plugin runtime, config, and docs behavior rather than a browser-rendered UI surface.\n",
